    "All 13 workflow jobs passed, including the cross-platform example WAV/PCM comparison.",
    "Windows Swift Debug and Release each listed 71 tests, executed 70, skipped 1 opt-in fixture generator test, and reported zero failures. macOS portable Debug and Release each listed 72, executed 71, skipped 1, and reported zero failures.",
    "Every shared Swift lane executed seven musical ruler tests and three portable ruler protocol tests covering tempo/signature changes, zero extent, density, resource bounds, recovered fixed/jump clock arithmetic, stale/external changes, read-only state and undo. Each also executed all nine authored CPR attachment/audition and checked-in source-fixture controls.",
    "All four normal-production-flag session helpers passed 52 interactive checks. The authored source-event journey now executes in every component lane, including explicit attachment, exact output/provenance hashes, rejection controls, undo/redo, save/reopen and original fixture preservation.",
    "All four process lanes checked 33 musical ruler ticks at 96 BPM/4/4 and 100 pixels per second: quarter notes at 0, 0.625, 1.25, 1.875 and 2.5 seconds, and bars at 0, 2.5, 5 and 7.5 seconds. Replies preserve full state and reject stale revisions.",
    "Each process lane checked exact source waveform extrema for 11 example clips and 17600 peak bins; the peak-word hash, ruler result and authored source export identity matched across all four lanes.",
    "Public macOS application tests listed 372, executed 255, skipped 117 private-fixture or opt-in generator tests, and reported zero failures.",
    "Windows C executed 5442 cases and 18380 checks per configuration; macOS C executed 5439 cases and 18324 checks per configuration. Both Windows native audio lifecycle lanes passed 89 checks. Public SoXR conversion API plumbing passed."
  ],
  "boundaries": [
